e baseline probe read the real source file at runtime (reported source_bytes 149, matching the frozen sample.py size) and called checkout_total(250, -3), which returned -750 (exit 0, claim_present true) instead of raising. The counterexample applied the identical probe to the same source text with only the contract guard inserted (patch_applied true); there the same call raised ValueError('quantity must not be negative') and claim_present was false (exit 0). Because the sole difference between the two runs is the presence of the negative-quantity check, the harness is not print-only, hard-coded, or always-true: it flips outcome with the source behavior, establishing that the unmodified code lacks validation. The negation ('checkout_total does validate quantity') is directly falsified by the baseline return value of -750.\",\"validation_verdict\":\"valid\"}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14101,"cache_read_input_tokens":1302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14101},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cff9b0a2-cd0a-43f9-ab63-f1188d90b6f8","uuid":"d79397d6-4b9f-4a5f-aa94-2fdd8ca006a8","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:31:02.475Z","request_id":"req_011CetGDaXYTGGT4MQ5BG1BD"},{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Output does not match required schema: root: must have required property 'finding_id', root: must have required property 'verdict', root: must have required property 'severity', root: must have required property 'usefulness', root: must have required property 'citations', root: must have required property 'counterexample', root: must have required property 'validation_verdict', root: must NOT have additional properties ('propert